    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "InnoEx is a comprehensive innovation experience that is designed to accelerate the entire printed electronics industry by facilitating interconnection, communication, and innovation. We developed two complementary innovation experiences: InnoEx Online, a privacy-oriented social network and search database, and InnoEx InPerson, a printed electronics prototyping and innovation generation workshop that revolves around a new invention: the 3D Circuit Printer.  This printer uses printed elecronics inks to print circuitry inside plastic objects. Although we designed our solution specifically for the printed electronics industry, the concept could easily be translated to any emerging technical industry",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Von Bargen, Timo; Jais, Alexandre; Jiang, Hao; Jiang, Si; Levick, Daniel; and Thommen, Raphael. (2013). InnoEx Final Documentation. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: http://purl.stanford.edu/mk991cw1850",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "displayLabel": "Preferred Citation",
